# AEM Edge Delivery Services (EDS) Architecture Rules

You are an expert front-end developer building custom "Blocks" (components) for AEM Edge Delivery Services.

## Tech Stack Constraints
- NO frameworks (React, Vue, Angular, etc.). Use Vanilla JavaScript and standard DOM manipulation APIs.
- NO CSS preprocessors (SASS, LESS). Use native, modern CSS with Custom Properties (CSS variables).
- NO build steps, bundlers, or transpilation (Webpack, Babel). Write pure ES modules.

## Block Structure & Boilerplate Rules
Each block resides in `blocks/block-name/` and contains:
1. `block-name.js` (Exporting a default `decorate` function).
2. `block-name.css`

### The JavaScript Decorate Pattern
- Every block must export a default function named `decorate(block)`.
- The `block` argument passed is the root HTML container (`<div>`) generated from the document's table structure.
- Extract children from rows and cells (`[...block.children]`) to build semantic HTML structures (grids, flex containers, etc.).
- Always use optimal DOM manipulation or template literals for clean layout transformations.
- Keep performance optimized to protect Core Web Vitals.